---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/**
 * The page that explains the bird. It is deliberately short: the pet is
 * already on this page, so the reader can try each thing as they read it.
 */

const interactions = [
  {
    action: 'Move your cursor',
    result:
      'Hawky follows. Small movements it ignores, medium ones it hops, longer ones it flies. Stop moving and it settles back into perching.',
  },
  {
    action: 'Click Hawky',
    result:
      'It goes to sleep and stops following. Click again and it startles awake. It will not take a click meant for a link or a button underneath it.',
  },
  {
    action: 'Double-click Hawky',
    result: 'It burns, collapses to ash, and is reborn. This takes about five seconds and cannot be interrupted.',
  },
  {
    action: 'Rest on Hawky',
    result: 'A small bubble appears with the time until the next rebirth.',
  },
  {
    action: 'Wait for the hour',
    result:
      'It burns on its own, once an hour, every hour. If you have put it to sleep it burns anyway and then goes back to sleep.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Hawky"
  description="The phoenix that lives on this site: what it does, and how to make it do it."
>
  <section class="column">
    <h1>Hawky</h1>

    <p class="lede mt-4">
      Hawky is a phoenix. It starts perched on the T of the wordmark at the top
      of the page, follows your cursor around, and burns itself to ash on the
      hour before rising again.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4">
      It is on every page of this site, including this one, so you can try each
      of these as you read.
    </p>

    <dl class="mt-10">
      {interactions.map((i) => (
        <div class="row">
          <dt>{i.action}</dt>
          <dd>{i.result}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <h2 class="mt-14">Every frame</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Forty-eight frames of 32 by 32 pixels, in four colours. Perching, leaving
      the ground, three flight angles, and the rebirth.
    </p>

    <figure class="sheet mt-6">
      <img
        src="/phoenix.png"
        alt="The Hawky sprite sheet: six rows of eight frames showing perching, hopping and taking off, three flight angles, and the rebirth cycle."
        width="256"
        height="192"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>

    <h2 class="mt-14">When it stays away</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Hawky never loads on a touch device, because there is no cursor to follow
      and it would sit in a corner looking broken. It also never loads if your
      system asks for reduced motion. It is a bird made entirely of movement, so
      it is removed rather than slowed down.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4">
      It renders behind the writing, so it can never cover a word you are
      reading. The one exception is the rebirth, which comes to the front for
      those few seconds.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  dl {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  /* Shown at 2x so the pixels stay square and countable rather than smoothed
     into a smear by the browser's default filtering. */
  .sheet {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink) 4%, transparent);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .sheet img {
    display: block;
    width: 512px;
    max-width: none;
    height: auto;
    image-rendering: pixelated;
  }
</style>
